  "goodToKnow": "Der Meteorit is a meteorite, a rock from space that reaches the ground; der Meteor is the streak of light in the sky, also die Sternschnuppe (shooting star). In 2002 the Neuschwanstein meteorite fell near the famous castle in Bavaria. The Nördlinger Ries, about 15 million years old, is one of Europe's best-preserved impact craters. It's declined weakly: den Meteoriten. Plural: die Meteoriten."
